            <ArticleTitle>Bilateral heel pain in a patient with Diamond-Blackfan anaemia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>110-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.foot.2015.03.002</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0958-2592(15)00011-5</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A rare case of bilateral calcaneal stress fractures in a patient with Diamond-Blackfan anaemia is described. This has not been previously reported in the literature. A calcaneal stress fracture is an important differential diagnosis in a patient presenting with heel pain. Bilaterality of symptoms should not exclude this diagnosis and clinicians should be especially vigilant with predisposed patients.</AbstractText>
